Product Requirements Document (PRD)
📌 Project Name

DataPilot AI – Smart Web Scraping & Analytics Dashboard

1. 🎯 Purpose

DataPilot AI is a web-based platform that allows users to:

Collect data from websites (automatically)

Analyze it using data science techniques

Visualize insights in a dashboard

Automate repetitive web-based tasks

The goal is to combine web scraping + data analysis + automation + visualization into one unified system.

2. 👥 Target Users

Students learning data science / Python

Job seekers (tracking job listings)

E-commerce researchers (price tracking)

General users who want automated insights

3. 🧩 Core Features
3.1 🔍 Data Input

Users can:

Enter a keyword or topic (e.g., “Python jobs in Lahore”)

Select data source type:

Jobs

Products

News

3.2 🕷️ Data Scraping Engine

Scrapes data from websites

Supports:

Static scraping (requests + BeautifulSoup)

Dynamic scraping (Selenium)

Functional Requirements:

Handle pagination

Extract structured fields (title, price, date, etc.)

Avoid duplicate entries

3.3 📊 Data Processing (Pandas)

Clean raw scraped data

Transform into structured datasets

Features:

Filtering (price range, location, etc.)

Aggregation (average, count)

Sorting & grouping

3.4 📈 Visualization Dashboard

Display processed data in charts

Charts:

Line charts (trends over time)

Bar charts (comparisons)

Pie charts (distribution)

UI:

Interactive dashboard (Flask templates + JS)

3.5 🤖 Automation System

Users can:

Schedule scraping jobs

Set conditions (e.g., price < X)

Actions:

Trigger alerts

Store historical data

3.6 🧱 OOP-Based Architecture

System structured with classes:

BaseScraper

JobScraper

ProductScraper

DataProcessor

Visualizer

AutomationManager

3.7 🖥️ Admin Panel (Tkinter)

Start/stop scraping jobs

Monitor logs

Manage tasks locally

4. 🌐 Technical Requirements
Backend

Python

Flask

Frontend

HTML, CSS, JavaScript

Data Handling

Pandas

Scraping

BeautifulSoup

Selenium

Visualization

Matplotlib / Plotly

GUI (Optional)

Tkinter

5. 🏗️ System Architecture
User Input (Web UI)
        ↓
Flask Backend
        ↓
Scraper Engine (BS4 / Selenium)
        ↓
Data Processing (Pandas)
        ↓
Database / Storage (CSV / SQLite)
        ↓
Visualization Engine
        ↓
Dashboard (Frontend)
6. 📦 Data Storage

Initial: CSV files

Advanced: SQLite database

7. ⚙️ Non-Functional Requirements

Scalable scraping design

Modular OOP code

Error handling (timeouts, broken pages)

Clean UI/UX

Maintainable codebase

8. 🚀 MVP Scope (First Version)

Include:

Single scraping category (e.g., jobs)

Basic dashboard

Manual scraping trigger

Simple charts

Exclude (for now):

Authentication

Advanced automation

Multi-user system

9. 🔮 Future Enhancements

User accounts & login

Cloud deployment

API integration

Real-time updates (AJAX/WebSockets)

Email notifications

Machine learning predictions

